<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Persistency of the contacts is done by the PersistentManifold class, and you can manage their lifetime yourself. No dynamic allocation is required if you use a cache of PersistentManifolds. </div></blockquote>Sounds good!<br><blockquote class="uncited"><div>I will have a look if it is doable to move ConvexConvexCollisionAlgorithm to the collision detection folder (it is a kind of bridge class at the moment). In that case you can use more of the framework.</div></blockquote>Yeah, I was thinking in order to do that you would have to move the contact processing down into the shape classes, or create a two tier wrapper system like the one I have, and move it up.<br><blockquote class="uncited"><div>By the way, can you share your broadphase ?</div></blockquote>Sure, I've been putting off uploading this to SourceForge but maybe you could give me some feedback in return?<br><br><a href="https://sourceforge.net/project/showfiles.php?group_id=113759" class="postlink">https://sourceforge.net/project/showfil ... _id=113759</a><br><a href="http://www.botworx.org" class="postlink">http://www.botworx.org</a><br><br>Thanks Erwin!<br><br>Kurtis<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=63">kfields</a> — Mon Aug 15, 2005 1:58 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
