		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=237#p237"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>All I need is a way to get contact points from bullet.</div></blockquote>In that case, it is probably best to just use the collision detection, which is located in the /Bullet/Bullet folder. You don't need any of the dynamics or integration files (ConvexConvexCollisionAlgorithm).<br><br>All you need it calling gjk, and pass the <br><div class="codebox"><p>Code: </p><pre><code>PersistentManifold* m_manifoldPtr;ManifoldResult output(body0,body1,m_manifoldPtr);GjkPairDetector::ClosestPointInput input;//init inputm_gjkPairDetector.GetClosestPoints(input,output);//the PersistentManifold class automatically manages the contact points, ManifoldResult passes contact points it gets from GJK.</code></pre></div>Persistency of the contacts is done by the PersistentManifold class, and you can manage their lifetime yourself. No dynamic allocation is required if you use a cache of PersistentManifolds.<br><br>I will have a look if it is doable to move ConvexConvexCollisionAlgorithm to the collision detection folder (it is a kind of bridge class at the moment). In that case you can use more of the framework.<br><br>By the way, can you share your broadphase ?<br><br>Thanks a lot for the feedback,<br>Erwin<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Sun Aug 14, 2005 8:03 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
