		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=230#p230"><![CDATA[
Hi,<br><br>It all depends, what you are looking for, but I would recommend to try to hook-up the Bullet collision detection to ODE.<br><br>Perhaps look at the module overview, or doxygen:<br>DOXYGEN: <br><a href="http://www.continuousphysics.com/Bullet/BulletFull/html/annotated.html" class="postlink">http://www.continuousphysics.com/Bullet ... tated.html</a> <br>MODULE OVERVIEW: <br><a href="http://www.continuousphysics.com/ftp/pub/test/BulletModules.pdf" class="postlink">http://www.continuousphysics.com/ftp/pu ... odules.pdf</a><br>ODE has more joints, and motors, Bullet only has ball-socket so far. Also Bullet lacks some optimizations like a kdop-tree for triangle meshes.<br>Benefit of Bullet is the unified convex collision detection, swept convex cast (swepth sphere, box), time of impact, and more understandable source code.<br><br>Would you be interested to try out to connect them together ?<br>Erwin<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Sat Aug 13, 2005 8:15 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
